# Missing or optional additions before the Astra Pro run

## Strongly recommended / materially missing

### 1. Current Paper B manuscript

Add the current PDF:

`Operator-Level Boolean Computation with Correspondence Matrices`

Preferably also add its current LaTeX/source and reproducibility supplement if available.

Why it matters: this is the hard scope boundary for what has already been developed in the CM/LM operator-computation paper. Astra should not count its CM representation, formula-valued LM calculus, valuation, logical pairing, signed operand-frame transformations, operator fusion, or compiler/folding foundations as new contributions of later papers unless a later theorem genuinely extends them.

### 2. Raw S1/S2 + matched benchmark package

If you have a ZIP/folder containing the actual later S1/S2 experiments and the matched four-arm Gate-A / Gate-P-style benchmark work, add it.

The package currently contains only the detailed prose interpretation of those results, plus an older illustrative folding benchmark inside the quantum handoff. The later raw code, seeds, per-case results, timing protocol, and output tables were not present as a standalone attachment in this thread.

Why it matters: the current scientific state is that pre-expansion folding can remove very large amounts of symbolic work on favorable structure, while a strong generic two-support optimizer reproduced the same final reductions in the tested S1/S2 families. The remaining high-value empirical question is whether CM's typed representation recognizes/executes those reductions faster or more cheaply under a controlled matched benchmark.

